DESCRIPTION:Use Your Common Sense Day is listed on November 4 by daily-holi
 day calendars that disagree with each other about who created it and canno
 t show where the date came from. November 4 does carry a real observance\,
  and a statutory one: Oklahoma has marked Will Rogers Day on that date sin
 ce 1947\, because it is the humorist's birthday. The link between Rogers a
 nd the common-sense day\, on the other hand\, exists only on the calendar 
 sites.\n\nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/use-your-common-sense-day/
